hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16170","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, my father narrated it to us from him while he was alive. He said: Hujr ibn al-Harith al-Ghassani of the people of al-Ramlah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Awf al-Kinani, and he was an agent of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz over al-Ramlah, that he witnessed Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan say to Bashir ibn Aqrabah al-Juhani on the day Amr ibn Said ibn al-As was killed: O Abu al-Yaman, I need today your speech, so stand and speak. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever stands preaching, seeking with it only show and repute, Allah Almighty will stop him on the Day of Resurrection in a station of show and repute."
